&Q000699 = A balbale to Ninŋišzida (Ninŋišzida A)
@composite
#project: etcslatf/inter
#atf: use unicode
#atf: use math
#etcsl: text-id=c.4.19.1
#key: after http://etcsl.orinst.ox.ac.uk/cgi-bin/etcsl.cgi?text=c.4.19.1&display=Crit&charenc=gcirc#

1. [ur]-saŋ en šag₄-tum₂ a-gar₃ ur-mah kur sud-[da]
#tr.en: Hero, lord of field and meadow, lion of the distant mountains! @wDN{Ninŋišzida},
#lem: ursaŋ[warrior]; en[lord]; šagtum[pasture land]; agar[meadow]; urmah[lion]; kur[mountain(s)]; sud[distant]
#etcsl: line-id=1

2. {d}nin-ŋiš-zid-da muš-mah ušumgal-a-da# [tab-ba]
#tr.en: who brings together giant snakes and dragons! Great wild bull who, in the murderous battle,
#lem: Ninŋešzidak[1]; mušmah[mythical creature]; ušumgal[great dragon]; tab[double]
#etcsl: line-id=2

3. am gal šen-šen-na gaba guz-a-ba a-ŋi₆ X [...]
#tr.en: is a flood that ……! Beloved by his mother, he to whom @wDN{Ningirida} gave birth from her luxurious body,
#lem: am[wild bull]; gal[big]; šen[battle]; gaba[breast]; guz[be crushed]; aŋi[wave]; X; X
#etcsl: line-id=3

4. ama-ni ki aŋ₂ {d}nin-girid₂-<da>-a šag₄ hi-li#-[a tud-da]
#tr.en: who drank the good milk at her holy breast, who sucked in lion's spittle, who grew up in the @fsux{abzu}!
#lem: ama[mother]; ki[place]; aŋ[measure]; Ningirida[1]DN; šag[heart]; hili[attractiveness]; utud[give birth (to)]
#etcsl: line-id=4

5. [ubur] kug-ga-na ga zid gu₇-a uš₁₁ piriŋ sub-sub-ba
#tr.en: August @fsux{išib} priest who holds the holy @fsux{ešda} vessels, checker of tablets, who secures justice ……!
#lem: ubur[breast]; kug[pure]; ga[milk]; zid[right]; gu[eat]; uš[poison]; piriŋ[lion]; sub[suck]
#etcsl: line-id=5

6. abzu-a buluŋ₃-ŋa₂ išib mah-am₃ eš₂-da kug šu du₈
#tr.en: King, wild bull with tall limbs (?), who directs speech aright, and who hates wickedness!
#lem: abzu[(cosmic) underground water]; buluŋ[grow]; išib[purification priest]; mah[great]; ešda[metal cultic vessel]; kug[purify]; šu[hand]; du[spread]
#etcsl: line-id=6

7. saŋ₅-ŋa₂ dub kalag-ga-ba niŋ₂-zid zu₂ keše₂-da
#tr.en: Mighty power,
#lem: saŋ[choose]; dub[tablet]; kalag[strong]; niŋzid[righteousness]; zu[tooth]; kešed[bind]
#etcsl: line-id=7

8. lugal am ur₅ un₃ eme si sa₂ niŋ₂-erim₂-e hul gig
#tr.en: whom no one dare stop when he spreads confusion!
#lem: lugal[king]; am[wild bull]; ur[root]; un[high]; eme[tongue]; si[horn]; sa[equal]; niŋerim[evil]; hulu[bad]; gig[sick]
#etcsl: line-id=8

9. uru₂ %s idim hur nu-mu-un-gi₄-gi₄ šu suh₃-a di-de₃
#tr.en: Mighty @wDN{Ninŋišzida},
#lem: uru[flood]; idim[heavy]; hur[ever (again)]; gi[turn]; šu[hand]; suh[confuse]; di[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=9

10. {d}nin-ŋiš-zid-da idim hur nu-mu-un-gi₄-gi₄ šu suh₃-a di-de₃
#tr.en: whom no one dare stop when he spreads confusion!
#lem: Ninŋešzidak[1]; idim[heavy]; hur[ever (again)]; gi[turn]; šu[hand]; suh[confuse]; di[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=10

11. erim-erim-ma šu-zu ma-ra-ši-ŋal₂
#tr.en: The troops are constantly at your service. Shepherd, you understand how to keep a check on the black-headed.
#lem: erin[people]; šu[hand]; ŋal[⟦be⟧ to be (there]
#etcsl: line-id=11

12. sipad saŋ gig₂-ga šid-bi mu-e-zu
#tr.en: The sheep and lambs come to seek you out,
#lem: sipad[shepherd]; saŋ[head]; giggig[black]; šid[count]; zu[know]
#etcsl: line-id=12

13. u₈ sila₄-bi kiŋ₂-kiŋ₂-de₃ ma-ra-ši-ŋen
#tr.en: and you understand how to wield the sceptre over the goats and kids, into the distant future.
#lem: u[sheep]; sila[lamb]; kiŋ[seek]; ŋen[go]
#etcsl: line-id=13

14. ud₅-de₃ maš₂-bi ŋidru ud su₃-ra₂ tum₂-tum₂-mu-bi mu-e-zu
#tr.en: @wDN{Ninŋišzida},
#lem: uzud[(female) goat]; maš[goat]; ŋidru[scepter]; ud[sun]; sud[distant]; tum[bring]; zu[know]
#etcsl: line-id=14

15. {d}nin-ŋiš-zid-da ŋidru ud su₃-ra₂ tum₂-tum₂-mu-bi mu-e-zu
#tr.en: you understand how to wield the sceptre, into the distant future.
#lem: Ninŋešzidak[1]; ŋidru[scepter]; ud[sun]; sud[distant]; tum[bring]; zu[know]
#etcsl: line-id=15

16. lugal šag₄-la₂ sug₄ šag₄-ta e₃-a inim šudu₃-zu šu-a he₂-eb-gi₄
#tr.en: The merciful king @noteref{i.e. Enki} entrusted you from your birth with your words of prayer.
#lem: lugal[king]; šala[pity]; sug[full]; šag[heart]; e[leave]; inim[word]; šud[prayer]; šu[hand]; gi[turn]
#etcsl: line-id=16

17. nam-til₃ u₃-tud za-da ša-mu-un-ŋal₂
#tr.en: He let you have life and creation. Prince endowed with attractiveness, @wDN{Ninŋišzida},
#lem: namtil[life]; utud[give birth (to)]; zaʾe[you]; ŋal[⟦be⟧ to be (there]
#etcsl: line-id=17

18. nun hi-li sud-sud {d}nin-ŋiš-zid-da
#tr.en: when taking your seat on the throne-dais in an elevated location, lord,
#lem: nun[prince]; hili[attractiveness]; sud[distant]; Ninŋešzidak[1]
#etcsl: line-id=18

19. barag# ki-tuš mah-a tuš-a-ni en diŋir šul a₂ zid-da
#tr.en: god, youth, right arm -- clothed in your ……,
#lem: barag[sanctum]; kituš[dwelling place]; mah[great]; tuš[sit (down)]; en[lord]; diŋir[deity]; šul[youth]; a[arm]; zid[right]
#etcsl: line-id=19

20. [...] X-zu-ur tug₂ mur₁₀ ŋidru za-gin₃ šu u₃-mu-e-ti
#tr.en: with the shining sceptre grasped in your hands -- then …… performs a @fsux{šir-namšub} song to you,
#lem: X; X; tug[textile]; mur[dress]; ŋidru[scepter]; zagin[lapis lazuli]; šu[hand]; teŋ[approach]
#etcsl: line-id=20

21. [šir₃]-nam#-šub ad mi-ri-ib-dug₄ ni₂-te-na mi-ni-ib#-[be₂]
#tr.en: addressing you intimately: @q[,Ninjiczida]{“
#lem: širnamšubak[subscript]; ad[voice]; dug[speak]; ni[self]; e[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=21

$ 1 line missing
23. [...]-bi# ka lul-la bal-bal-[am₃ šag₄] mu-na-te-en-[te-en]
#tr.en: You bring calming of the heart to …… who …… lies.
#lem: X; kag[mouth]; lul[false]; bala[turn]; šag[heart]; ten[extinguish]
#etcsl: line-id=23

24. [...] X šar₂-šar₂-ra ša-mu-šub{ub}-be₂-en izi-gin₇ ba-ra-ma₅-ma₅-an
#tr.en: You fall upon the many …… and you burn them like fire.”}
#lem: X; X; šar[numerous]V/i; šub[fall]; izi[fire]; ma[burn]
#etcsl: line-id=24

25. lugal en šag₄ su₃-ra₂ barag mah-za nam dug₃ mu-ri-in-tar
#tr.en: The king who is the lord of broad understanding @noteref{i.e. Enki} has determined a good destiny for you on your elevated throne-dais;
#lem: lugal[king]; en[lord]; šag[heart]; sud[distant]; barag[sanctum]; mah[great]; nam[fate]; dug[good]; tar[cut]
#etcsl: line-id=25

26. diŋir niŋ₂-si-sa₂-e ki aŋ₂-e inim dug₃-bi mu-un-e
#tr.en: the god who loves justice @noteref{probably Utu} has spoken these favourable words: @q[Utu,Ninjiczida]{“Foremost one,
#lem: diŋir[deity]; niŋsisa[justice]; ki[place]; aŋ[measure]; inim[word]; dug[good]; dug[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=26

27. palil gal-zu unken-na PA-PA-a he₂-du₇
#tr.en: leader of the assembly, glory of ……, king endowed with awesomeness,
#lem: palil[first and foremost]; galanzu[wise]; unkin[assembly]; X; hedu[ornament]
#etcsl: line-id=27

28. lugal ni₂ ri-a ildum₂ ud-bi saŋ-ba du-a
#tr.en: sun of the masses, advancing in front of them! Who can rival you in the highest heaven?
#lem: lugal[king]; ni[fear]; ri[impose]; ildum[band]; ud[sun]; saŋ[head]; ŋen[go]
#etcsl: line-id=28

29. an-bar an-ta a-ba de-ŋen-ne₂ a-na an-da-sa₂-a
#tr.en: What can equal you?”} Hero who, after surveying the battle, goes up to the high mountains!
#lem: anbar[the side of heaven]; an[sky]; aba[who?]; ŋen[go]; ana[what?]; sa[equal]
#etcsl: line-id=29

30. ur-saŋ me₃ igi ŋal₂ taka₄-a kur un₃-na i₃-a-e₃
#tr.en: @wDN{Ninŋišzida}, who, after surveying the battle, goes up to the high mountains!
#lem: ursaŋ[warrior]; me[battle]; igi[eye]; ŋal[open]; taka[set aside]; kur[mountain(s)]; un[high]; e[leave]
#etcsl: line-id=30

31. {d}nin-ŋiš-zid-da me₃ igi ŋal₂ taka₄-a kur un₃-na i₃-a-e₃
#tr.en: King, you who carry out commands in the great underworld,
#lem: Ninŋešzidak[1]; me[battle]; igi[eye]; ŋal[open]; taka[set aside]; kur[mountain(s)]; un[high]; e[leave]
#etcsl: line-id=31

32. lugal ki gu-la a₂ aŋ₂-ŋa₂ tum₂ ki DU-bi tum₂-mu-de₃
#tr.en: you who carry out the underworld's business!
#lem: lugal[king]; ki[place]; gal[big]; a[arm]; aŋ[measure]; tum[carry]; ki[place]; X; tum[bring]
#etcsl: line-id=32

33. šul diŋir tuku ki a₂ aŋ₂-ŋa₂-ni igi-bi ma-ra-ši-ŋal₂
#tr.en: Any youth who has a personal god is at your disposal, there where your commands are issued.
#lem: šul[youth]; diŋir[deity]; tuku[acquire]; ki[place]; a[arm]; aŋ[measure]; igi[eye]; ŋal[⟦be⟧ to be (there]
#etcsl: line-id=33

34. lugal ka lal₃ diŋir-re-e-ne {d}en-ki za₃-mi₂
#tr.en: O king, honeyed mouth of the gods!
#lem: lugal[king]; kag[mouth]; lal[syrup]; diŋir[deity]; Enkik[1]DN; zamin[praise]
#etcsl: line-id=34

35. {d}nin-ŋiš-zid-da dumu {d}nin-a-zu
#tr.en: Praise be to @wDN{Enki}. @wDN{Ninŋišzida}, son of @wDN{Ninazu}!
#lem: Ninŋešzidak[1]; dumu[child]; Ninazu[1]DN
#etcsl: line-id=35

36. a-a {d}en-ki za₃-mi₂
#tr.en: Praise be to Father @wDN{Enki}.
#lem: aya[father]; Enkik[1]DN; zamin[praise]
#etcsl: line-id=36

@div trailer 

37. bal-bal-e {d}nin-ŋiš-zid-da-kam
#tr.en: A @fsux{balbale} of @wDN{Ninŋišzida}.
#lem: balbale[literary subscript]; Ninŋešzidak[1]
#etcsl: line-id=37

@end trailer







